File Index

/command-shortcuts.md
Purpose: This file documents command shortcuts and speedwalking features for the Shattered Archive MUD client.

/definitions.md
Purpose: This file defines key technical terms and architectural components used throughout the Shattered Archive project.

/deploy.md
Purpose: This file explains the internal deployment architecture including Docker, TLS, and nginx routing for the ShatteredArchive project.

/dictation.md
Purpose: Enables reliable, client-side voice dictation for MUD-style game commands.

/docker.md
Purpose: This file documents the Docker-based local development environment for ShatteredArchive.

/game-client.md
Purpose: This file documents the Shattered Archive MUD client's architecture, scripting support, and event system.

/game-server.md
Purpose: This file documents the protocol and configuration for a WebSocket-to-Telnet proxy server that bridges browser clients to MUD games.

/ports.md
Purpose: This file indexes application ports for different project components.

/scrum-poker-user-guide.md
Purpose: End-user guide for Scrum Poker, written for the people ESTIMATING rather than the people running the stack — quick start, how a round works, reading the three estimate-column states, the buttons, organizer settings, and a symptom-to-action troubleshooting table. Deliberately free of ports, env vars and API routes; those live in scrum-poker.md, which this links to at the bottom.

/scrum-poker.md
Purpose: Guide to the Scrum Poker app (scrum-poker.shatteredarchive.dev) — the three packages and ports, local dev commands, how server-enforced vote hiding and the two possession-based identities (room code = membership, host token = organizer) work, the idle/TTL timeouts and the behaviours that depend on them, storage, the single opt-in ad slot, the HTTP API, and deployment.

/web-client.md
Purpose: This file indexes the web client module's overview, location, and server connections.

/web-server.md
Purpose: This file documents the web server's API endpoints, caching strategy, and integration with the Shattered Archive remote server for map data retrieval.
